<article class="env-lemma" id="0G1G">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G1G">Lemma <span data-tag="0G1G">58.32.2</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p > 0$. Let $X \to \mathbf{A}^ n_ k$ be an étale morphism with $X$ affine. Then there exists a finite étale morphism $X \to \mathbf{A}^ n_ k$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Write $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(C)$. Set $A = 0$ and denote $I = k[x_1, \ldots , x_ n]$. By assumption there exists some étale $k$-algebra map $\varphi : k[x_1, \ldots , x_ n] \to C$. Denote $\tau : C/\varphi (I)C \to 0$ the unique surjection. We may choose $\varphi $ and $\tau $ such that $N(C, \varphi , \tau )$ is minimal. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0G1F" data-tag="0G1F">58.32.1</a> we get $N(C, \varphi , \tau ) = 0$. Hence $\varphi $ is finite étale. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>